        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(browser): remove hardcoded profile=\"user\" suggestion from tool description",
        "body": "Fixes #102566\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe browser tool description hardcoded a suggestion to use `profile=\"user\"` even when the operator has configured `browser.defaultProfile: \"openclaw\"`. This caused model confusion on setups where the `openclaw` profile uses CDP direct attach and the `user` profile (Chrome MCP transport) fails to connect.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe hardcoded `profile=\"user\"` text in the tool description contradicted project context (MEMORY.md) that instructs agents to never use the `user` profile. The fix generalizes the guidance to reference the configured `browser.defaultProfile` setting instead of prescribing a specific profile value.\n\n## User Impact\n\n**Before:** Browser tool description always said `use profile=\"user\"` regardless of config, causing model confusion.\n**After:** Description references `browser.defaultProfile` (e.g. `openclaw` for CDP attach or `user` for Chrome MCP transport).\n\n## Evidence\n- `git diff --check` clean\n- Updated browser-tool.test.ts assertion to match new wording\n- 2 files changed (plugin-registration.ts + test)",
        "branch": "fix/browser-user-profile-suggestion-102566",
